@startuml seq-07-owner-send-concurrent
!include style.iuml
title The owner's Send from Settings, concurrent with an agent's payment from the same wallet\none lane, queue-commit order, one nonce in flight (C1, C2, C5, C11, C14; H-132, H-164, H-254; NonceAlloc)
autonumber "<b>0."

actor Owner
participant "Web app\nSettings → Wallets → Send" as Web
participant "Agent Mara\n(model)" as Agent
participant "Daemon\n(API, wallet~__send)" as D
database "Store" as Store
participant "Wallet lane W" as Lane
participant "Signer" as Signer
participant "RPC / Base" as Chain

par
  Owner -> Web : Send 10 USDC to Ana (the review opened with clientRequestId r)
  Web -> D : POST send {to, amount, token, r, version}
  D -> Store : queue commit q1: owner payment O (payer owner: owner authority, no rule),\nreservation 10 USDC + fees
  note right of Store : row: payment Idle · call [wallet_usable and payer == 'owner' and fits] → Queued
else
  Agent -> D : wallet~__send {to: Bob, amount: "4"} (Bob is Always for Mara)
  D -> Store : admission commit q2: agent payment A, reservation 4 USDC + fees;\nthe available balance already counts O's reservation (C11)
  note right of Store : row: payment Idle · call [... eff == 'always' and fits] → Queued
end
note over D, Store
  The store has one commit line: q1 and q2 are ordered, and the later sees the earlier (C1).
  Say q1 < q2. Had the balance been under 14 USDC plus fees, the later one would be refused at
  the call with the available amount, no draft (OD-8; Idle · call [... not fits] → Refused).
end note

opt the owner taps Send twice
  Web -> D : POST send {..., r}
  D --> Web : the same payment O (C14: the client request id is the key)
end

Lane -> Store : head of the FIFO: O (the Send never jumps the queue, nor is jumped: C2)
note right of Lane : nonce · lane_turn [queued and can_sign and not chain_ahead] → signing
Lane -> Signer : sign O at nonce n
Signer --> Lane : raw O
Lane -> Store : start commit O: nonce n burnt, Signed
note right of Store : nonce · start_commit [not ledger_moved and recheck_ok] → in_flight
Lane -> Chain : broadcast O's stored bytes
note over Lane
  One in flight (C5, R-10): A waits until O is Included at latest.
  nonce · included_latest [more_in_flight] → in_flight stays, else → free.
end note
Chain --> Lane : receipt O at latest
Lane -> Store : O Included; nonce lease released
note right of Store : nonce · included_latest [not more_in_flight] → free
Lane -> Signer : sign A at nonce n+1
Signer --> Lane : raw A
Lane -> Store : start commit A: re-check Always(Mara, W, Bob), balance; nonce n+1, Signed
Lane -> Chain : broadcast A's stored bytes
Chain --> Lane : receipt A at latest
Lane -> Store : A Included
note over Owner, Chain
  From a paired phone the owner sends only to recipients the wallet knows; a new address is confirmed on the host (OD-3).
  An owner's cancel or speed-up of a payment already in the lane enters it as a command, so the lane stays the only writer
  of the wallet's nonces (C2). An archive committed before q1 refuses the Send (H-047, C17).
end note
@enduml
